From: cyy <cyyever@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: append CEF flags to steamwebhelper.exe

Steam's CEF host steamwebhelper.exe crashes under Wine on macOS without two
Chromium flags:

  - --no-sandbox: CEF's sandbox hooks the NT kernel and, under Wine's
    incomplete sandbox emulation, deadlocks its own cross-thread IPC
    (src/common/pipes.cpp "Stalled cross-thread pipe" -> Fatal assert ->
    _ExitOnFatalAssert; the host exits).

  - --in-process-gpu: the out-of-process GPU process cannot create an
    ANGLE/D3D11 window surface on the browser window under Wine+DXMT
    (eglCreateWindowSurface failed; SwapChain11.cpp), so the UI never paints.
    Running the GPU in-process sidesteps the cross-process surface.

NOTE: the GPU process's SharedImageStub (GPU virtualization) requires a shared
GLES3 context. ANGLE's D3D11 backend only reaches GLES3 when d3d11 is DXMT
(Metal, feature level 11_1); the Wine builtin wined3d caps at feature level
9_3 (macOS GL 2.1, no core context) -> GLES2 only -> "Failed to create shared
context for virtualization" retry loop. So this flag assumes DXMT is installed
as the d3d11 builtin (`make dxmt`); `make proton` alone reinstalls wined3d's
d3d11 and must be followed by `make dxmt` (build-proton-x86.sh now restores
DXMT over wined3d after install to make this order-independent).

  - --use-angle=swiftshader: ANGLE's default D3D11 backend cannot create a
    window surface under Wine — eglCreateWindowSurface fails with EGL_BAD_ALLOC
    after SwapChain11::reset reports "Could not create additional swap chains or
    offscreen surfaces" (HRESULT 0x80004005). The window frame appears but its
    contents never paint. Reproduced with an unmodified upstream Chromium in the
    same bottle: the default backend logs one EGL_BAD_ALLOC, while
    --use-angle=swiftshader and --disable-gpu log none. SwiftShader renders in
    software, which is enough for a 2D store/login UI and avoids the surface
    allocation entirely. (DirectComposition is also unimplemented in Wine —
    DCompositionCreateDevice3 returns E_NOTIMPL — but that is not the cause:
    Chromium falls back from it correctly, and the fallback is what fails.)

Whisky previously injected the flags via an IFEO "Debugger" wrapper around
steamwebhelper.exe (steamwebhelper_wrapper.exe + a steamwebhelper_real.exe copy
+ a per-bottle registry value, on top of patch 0010's IFEO-debugger support).
That is a lot of machinery for two flags. Wine already has a
hack_append_command_line() table that appends flags per-exe (Warhammer2.exe and
SummerIslands.exe already get --in-process-gpu there), so this adds a
steamwebhelper.exe entry instead. The substring match catches every
steamwebhelper.exe launch (browser + renderer/gpu/utility children), matching
the prior wrapper's behavior, and lets us delete the wrapper binary, the _real
copy, the IFEO registry setup, and the Steam.swift plumbing for it.

---
diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
@@ -617,6 +617,7 @@ static const WCHAR *hack_append_command_line( const WCHAR *cmd )
         {L"Red Tie Runner.exe", L" --use-angle=gl"},
         {L"UnrealCEFSubProcess.exe", L" --use-gl=swiftshader", "2316580"},
         {L"UnrealCEFSubProcess.exe", L" --use-angle=d3d9", "2684500"},
+        {L"steamwebhelper.exe", L" --no-sandbox --in-process-gpu --use-angle=swiftshader"},
     };
     unsigned int i;
     char sgi[64];
